Hi all!

Is there anyone currently working on SuSE 9.0 support for SELinux? I
will begin to work on this shortly but would like to avoid duplicate
work if possible.
I am aware that Carsten Grohmann and Paul Dwerryhouse have made RPMs for
SuSE in the past and will look at these.

I'd be very interested in hearing about any gotchas, things to watch out
for when packaging SELinux userland as I don't have very much experience
with RPM or the changes made by SuSE to the respective packages.

